 Here we use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality to find the maximum value of the given expression. By the triangle inequality, we have
\begin{align*}
\|\mathbf{a} - 2 \mathbf{b}\|^2 + \|\mathbf{b} - 2 \mathbf{c}\|^2 + \|\mathbf{c} - 2 \mathbf{a}\|^2 & \leq \|\mathbf{a}\|^2 + 4 \|\mathbf{b}\|^2 + \|\mathbf{b}\|^2 + 4 \|\mathbf{c}\|^2 + \|\mathbf{c}\|^2 + 4 \|\mathbf{a}\|^2\\
& = 5 + 4 \cdot 1 + 4 + 4 \cdot 4 + 4 + 4 \cdot 1\\
& = 41.
\end{align*}
